                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The best method to measure HbA1c is option A, isoelectric focusing.\n\nIsoelectric focusing is a technique that separates proteins based on their isoelectric point, which is the pH at which the protein has no net charge. HbA1c is a glycated form of hemoglobin, which means that glucose has attached to the hemoglobin molecule. This changes the isoelectric point of the hemoglobin, allowing it to be separated from other forms of hemoglobin using isoelectric focusing.\n\nAffinity chromatography, ion exchange chromatography, and electrophoresis are all techniques that can be used to separate proteins, but they are not as specific for HbA1c as isoelectric focusing. Therefore, option A is the best method to measure HbA1c.",
