                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand what phase 1 clinical trials are\nPhase 1 clinical trials are the first stage of testing a new drug or treatment in humans. They are usually conducted on a small group of healthy volunteers to evaluate the safety, tolerability, and pharmacokinetics (how the drug is absorbed, distributed, metabolized, and eliminated by the body) of the drug.\n\nStep 2: Identify the major aim of phase 1 clinical trials\nBased on the definition above, we can see that the major aim of phase 1 clinical trials is to evaluate the safety of the drug. Therefore, the correct answer is A) Safety. \n\nNote: While dose and pharmacokinetics are important aspects of phase 1 clinical trials, they are not the major aim. Efficacy is not typically evaluated in phase 1 clinical trials as the focus is on safety and tolerability.",
