                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nB) Concussion is the most likely cause in this scenario. The history of fall and vomiting near an alcohol shop suggest a head injury, and the symptoms of being awake with open eyes and retrograde amnesia are consistent with a concussion. Diffuse axonal injury and cerebral venous thrombosis are more severe and less common causes of head injury, and drunkenness alone would not cause these symptoms. However, it is important to perform a thorough evaluation and imaging studies to rule out other potential causes.",
