                        "cot": "\n1. Raw eggs contain a protein called avidin which binds biotin and makes it unavailable for the body.\n2. Biotin is a cofactor for carboxylase enzymes.\n3. Avidin is denatured by cooking.\n4. Therefore, the person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n5. Biotin is a cofactor for carboxylase enzymes.\n6. Therefore, the person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n7. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n8. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n9. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n10. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n11. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n12. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n13. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n14. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n15. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n16. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n17. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n18. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n19. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n20. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n21. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n22. The person is suffering from biotin deficiency.\n\nAnswer:\nThe person is suffering from biotin deficiency.",
