                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Golgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in the tendons of skeletal muscles. They are responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are Golgi tendon organs?\n2. Where are Golgi tendon organs located?\n3. What do Golgi tendon organs detect?\n4. Is it static or dynamic muscle length that Golgi tendon organs detect?\n5. Is it muscle tension or muscle action that Golgi tendon organs detect?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Golgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in the tendons of skeletal muscles.\n2. Golgi tendon organs are located in the tendons of skeletal muscles near their attachment to the muscle fibers.\n3. Golgi tendon organs detect changes in muscle tension.\n4. Golgi tendon organs do not detect static or dynamic muscle length. They detect changes in muscle tension.\n5. Golgi tendon organs detect muscle tension, not muscle action.",
                        "answers": [
