                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand what Golgi tendon organs are\nGolgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in the tendons of muscles. They are responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the answer choices\nA) Static muscle length - This answer choice is incorrect because Golgi tendon organs do not detect static muscle length.\nB) Dynamic muscle length - This answer choice is incorrect because Golgi tendon organs do not detect dynamic muscle length.\nC) Muscle tension - This answer choice is correct because Golgi tendon organs detect changes in muscle tension.\nD) Muscle action - This answer choice is incorrect because Golgi tendon organs do not detect muscle action.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is C) Muscle tension.\n\nFinal answer: Golgi tendon organs detect muscle tension.",
