                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nwe need to calculate the net filtration pressure (NFP):\n\nNFP = capillary hydrostatic pressure - interstitial hydrostatic pressure - capillary oncotic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure\n\nGiven that NFP = 3 mm Hg, interstitial hydrostatic pressure = 2 mm Hg, and interstitial oncotic pressure = 7 mm Hg, we can rearrange the equation to solve for capillary oncotic pressure:\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = capillary hydrostatic pressure - interstitial hydrostatic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure - NFP\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = 25 mm Hg - 2 mm Hg + 7 mm Hg - 3 mm Hg\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = 27 mm Hg\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 27.",
