                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nNet filtration pressure = (capillary hydrostatic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure) - (capillary oncotic pressure + interstitial hydrostatic pressure)\n\nWe are given the values of interstitial hydrostatic pressure (2 mm Hg), interstitial oncotic pressure (7 mm Hg), and capillary hydrostatic pressure (25 mm Hg). We need to find the capillary oncotic pressure to allow a net filtration pressure of 3 mm Hg.\n\nRearranging the equation, we get:\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = (capillary hydrostatic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure) - (interstitial hydrostatic pressure + net filtration pressure)\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = (25 mm Hg + 7 mm Hg) - (2 mm Hg + 3 mm Hg)\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = 27 mm Hg - 5 mm Hg\n\nCapillary oncotic pressure = 22 mm Hg\n\nTherefore, the answer is not given in the options. The correct answer is 22 mm Hg.",
