                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's recall the formula for net filtration pressure (NFP):\n\nNFP = (capillary hydrostatic pressure - interstitial hydrostatic pressure) - (capillary oncotic pressure - interstitial oncotic pressure)\n\nWe are given the following values:\n\n- Interstitial hydrostatic pressure = 2 mm Hg\n- Interstitial oncotic pressure = 7 mm Hg\n- Capillary hydrostatic pressure = 25 mm Hg\n- Net filtration pressure = 3 mm Hg\n\nWe need to find the capillary oncotic pressure (COP). Let's plug in the given values into the formula and solve for COP:\n\n3 = (25 - 2) - (COP - 7)\n\n3 = 23 - (COP - 7)\n\nNow, let's simplify the equation and solve for COP:\n\n3 + COP - 7 = 23\n\nCOP - 4 = 23\n\nCOP = 27\n\nSo, the capillary oncotic pressure should be 27 mm Hg. The correct answer is D) 27.",
