                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Calculate the net filtration pressure (NFP)\nNFP = capillary hydrostatic pressure - interstitial hydrostatic pressure - capillary oncotic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure\nNFP = 25 - 2 - capillary oncotic pressure + 7\nNFP = 30 - capillary oncotic pressure\n\nStep 2: Set the NFP to the given value of 3 mm Hg and solve for capillary oncotic pressure\nNFP = 3\n30 - capillary oncotic pressure = 3\ncapillary oncotic pressure = 27\n\nTherefore, the capillary oncotic pressure should be 27 mm Hg to allow a net filtration pressure of 3 mm Hg. The answer is D) 27.",
