                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe cortex of a lymph node is the outer layer, and it contains lymphatic nodules, which are clusters of lymphocytes and macrophages. These nodules are important for filtering and trapping foreign substances, such as bacteria and viruses.\n\nThe cords of Billroth are found in the spleen, not in lymph nodes. They are a network of reticular fibers and macrophages that help filter blood.\n\nHassall's corpuscles are found in the thymus gland, not in lymph nodes. They are clusters of epithelial cells that help regulate the development of T cells.\n\nWhite pulp is found in the spleen, not in lymph nodes. It is a region of the spleen that contains lymphocytes and is involved in immune function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Lymphatic nodules.",
