                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what the first pass effect is. The first pass effect refers to the metabolism of a drug that occurs in the liver and gut wall before it enters the systemic circulation. This means that some of the drug is broken down and eliminated before it even reaches the rest of the body.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) First pass effect.",
