                        "cot": " After a drug is administered, it enters the body. The body then starts to break down and eliminate the drug. This process is called elimination. The drug is eliminated before it enters the systemic circulation. The first pass effect is the process by which the amount of a drug in the body decreases after administration, but before entering the systemic circulation.",
