                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Define each option to understand their meanings.\n2. Eliminate options that do not fit the description.\n3. Choose the option that best fits the description.\n\n1. Definitions:\nA) Excretion - the process by which a drug or its metabolites are eliminated from the body.\nB) First pass effect - the initial metabolism of a drug by the liver before it enters the systemic circulation.\nC) First order elimination - the rate of elimination of a drug is proportional to the concentration of the drug in the body.\nD) Metabolism - the process by which a drug is chemically altered in the body.\n\n2. Elimination:\nOption A - Excretion: This option does not fit the description as it refers to the elimination of a drug from the body after it has entered the systemic circulation.\nOption C - First order elimination: This option does not fit the description as it refers to the rate of elimination of a drug, not the process by which the drug is eliminated before entering the systemic circulation.\nOption D - Metabolism: This option does not fit the description as it refers to the chemical alteration of a drug in the body, not the process by which the drug is eliminated before entering the systemic circulation.\n\n3. Answer:\nOption B - First pass effect: This option best fits the description as it refers to the initial metabolism of a drug by the liver before it enters the systemic circulation.",
