                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) 2-6 years.\n\nPiaget's theory of cognitive development includes four stages, and the preoperational stage is the second stage. During this stage, children develop symbolic thinking and language skills, but they still struggle with logical reasoning and understanding the perspectives of others.\n\nThe preoperational stage typically occurs between the ages of 2 and 6 years old. Therefore, option C) 2-6 years is the correct answer. \n\nOption A) Birth to 18 months is incorrect because this period is part of the sensorimotor stage, which is the first stage of Piaget's theory.\n\nOption B) 12 years onwards is incorrect because this period is part of the formal operational stage, which is the fourth and final stage of Piaget's theory.\n\nOption D) 7-12 years is incorrect because this period is part of the concrete operational stage, which is the third stage of Piaget's theory.",
