                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Cataract extraction surgery is a common procedure to remove the cloudy lens from the eye and replace it with an artificial one. Post-operative vision effects are important to evaluate to ensure the success of the surgery and to identify any complications.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is PCB?\n2. What are the common post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery?\n3. What is active surveillance?\n4. What is sentinel surveillance?\n5. What is passive surveillance?\n6. What is routine checkup of all operated cases?\n\nAnswers:\n1. PCB stands for Primary Care-Based.\n2. Common post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery include blurred vision, sensitivity to light, and mild discomfort.\n3. Active surveillance involves actively seeking out and monitoring cases of a particular condition or disease.\n4. Sentinel surveillance involves monitoring a specific group of people who are at high risk for a particular condition or disease.\n5. Passive surveillance involves relying on healthcare providers to report cases of a particular condition or disease.\n6. Routine checkup of all operated cases involves scheduling regular follow-up appointments with patients who have undergone cataract extraction surgery to monitor their vision and identify any complications.\n\nBased on the information provided, the answer to the original question is D) Routine checkup of all operated cases.",
