                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking about the method used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nStep 2: Understand the options\nA) Active surveillance: This involves actively seeking out cases of a particular disease or condition.\nB) Sentinel surveillance: This involves monitoring a specific group of people who are at high risk for a particular disease or condition.\nC) Passive surveillance: This involves relying on healthcare providers to report cases of a particular disease or condition.\nD) Routine checkup of all operated cases: This involves regularly checking on all patients who have undergone cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nStep 3: Eliminate options\nOption A and B do not seem relevant to the question as they are more focused on disease surveillance rather than evaluating post-operative vision effects. Option D seems like a reasonable option, but it is not specific to PCB. Therefore, we can eliminate options A, B, and D.\n\nStep 4: Choose the answer\nThe only option left is C) Passive surveillance, which involves relying on healthcare providers to report cases of a particular disease or condition. This seems like the most appropriate option for evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nAnswer: C) Passive surveillance.",
