                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Understand what a reverse bevel incision is.\n2. Identify the purpose of a reverse bevel incision.\n3. List the possible reasons for making a reverse bevel incision.\n4. Evaluate each option against the purpose of a reverse bevel incision.\n5. Choose the option that best fits the purpose.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. A reverse bevel incision is a type of incision made in periodontal surgery where the incision is made from the gingival margin towards the alveolar crest.\n2. The purpose of a reverse bevel incision is to provide access to the alveolar crest and remove infected tissue in the sulcus while allowing atraumatic reflection of the gingival margin.\n3. The possible reasons for making a reverse bevel incision are:\n- To remove infected tissue in the sulcus\n- To provide access to the alveolar crest\n- To allow atraumatic reflection of the gingival margin\n4. Evaluating each option against the purpose of a reverse bevel incision:\n- Option A: Allowing atraumatic reflection of the gingival margin fits the purpose of a reverse bevel incision.\n- Option B: Removing infected tissue in the sulcus fits the purpose of a reverse bevel incision.\n- Option C: Providing access to the alveolar crest fits the purpose of a reverse bevel incision.\n- Option D: All of the above options fit the purpose of a reverse bevel incision.\n5. Therefore, the correct answer is D) All of the above.",
