                        "cot": "\n\nC) Posterior cruciate ligament\n\nThe presentation of instability in full extension without instability at 90 degrees of flexion is a classic sign of a posterior cruciate ligament (PCL) injury. The PCL is the primary stabilizer of the knee in full extension, and its injury can lead to posterior translation of the tibia relative to the femur. The other structures listed are not typically associated with this specific presentation of knee instability.",
