                        "cot": " First, we need to calculate the change in intrapleural pressure. This is done by subtracting the intrapleural pressure before inspiration (-4 cm of water) from the intrapleural pressure after inspiration (-9 cm of water). This gives us a change in intrapleural pressure of -5 cm of water.\n\nNext, we need to calculate the pulmonary compliance. This is done by dividing the tidal volume (500 mL) by the change in intrapleural pressure (-5 cm of water). This gives us a pulmonary compliance of 0.2 L/cm.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 0.2 L/cm.",
