                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The tidal volume is the amount of air that the patient inhales in one breath. The intrapleural pressure is the pressure in the pleural cavity, which is the space between the lungs and the chest wall. The difference between the two pressures is the amount of air that the lungs can expand. The compliance is the amount of air that the lungs can expand per unit of pressure.\n\nThe difference between the intrapleural pressure before and after inspiration is 5 cm of water. This is the amount of air that the lungs can expand. The compliance is the amount of air that the lungs can expand per unit of pressure. In this case, the compliance is 5 cm of water/500 mL, or 0.01 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "7cc80ab3-c3d0-4bf1-b2c3-2e1f4e32d4e9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
