                    {
                        "id": "fa64e5f2-c6f0-41ff-8473-f915ada3bf2c",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-05",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThis question is difficult. \n\nPulmonary compliance can be calculated using the formula: \n\nCompliance = change in volume / change in pressure \n\nIn this case, the change in volume is the tidal volume of 500 mL. The change in pressure is the difference between the intrapleural pressure before and after inspiration, which is 5 cm of water (since -4 - (-9) = 5). \n\nConverting cm of water to cm of airway pressure, we get: \n\n5 cm H2O x 0.74 cm H2O/cm airway pressure = 3.7 cm airway pressure \n\nTherefore, the pulmonary compliance can be calculated as: \n\nCompliance = 500 mL / 3.7 cm H2O = 135 mL/cm H2O \n\nConverting mL/cm H2O to L/cm, we get: \n\nCompliance = 0.135 L/cm \n\nRounding to one decimal place, the answer is C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
