                        "cot": "Surgical labyinthectomy is a surgery to remove the labyrinth. The labyrinth is the organ of balance. Vestibular neurectomy is a surgery to remove the vestibular nerve. The vestibular nerve is the nerve that controls the balance of the body. The vestibular nerve controls the balance of the body in menieres disease. The best surgery to relieve intractable veigo in a menieres disease patient is B. So, the answer is B.",
