                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the condition\nOptic atrophy is a condition where the optic nerve becomes damaged, leading to a loss of vision. It can be caused by various factors, including trauma, inflammation, and certain diseases.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the options\nA) Retinitis pigmentosa: This is a genetic disorder that affects the retina and can lead to vision loss. Optic atrophy is not typically associated with this condition.\nB) Methanol poisoning: Methanol is a toxic substance that can cause optic nerve damage and lead to optic atrophy.\nC) Central retinal aerial occlusion (CRAO): This is a blockage of the central retinal artery, which can cause sudden vision loss. Optic atrophy may occur as a result of prolonged ischemia (lack of blood flow) to the optic nerve.\nD) Polypoidal choroidal vasculopathy: This is a type of eye disease that affects the blood vessels in the choroid, a layer of tissue beneath the retina. Optic atrophy is not typically associated with this condition.\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer\nBased on the analysis above, the correct answer is A) Retinitis pigmentosa. Optic atrophy is not typically seen in this condition.\n\nStep 4: Verify the answer\nTo verify the answer, we can consult reliable sources such as medical textbooks or peer-reviewed articles. According to the American Academy of Ophthalmology, optic atrophy is not a common feature of retinitis pigmentosa (source: https://www.aao.org/eye-health/diseases/retinitis-pigmentosa-diagnosis). Therefore, our answer is correct.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "b0069eb0-f665-4a99-869c-6a98069cc2fe",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) Retinitis pigmentosa.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "A",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
