                    {
                        "id": "33b0241a-81fe-4996-bec1-15f9a44be875",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Assess the situation and ensure your own safety.\nBefore approaching the patient, make sure the scene is safe for you to approach. Look for any potential hazards or dangers that could put you or the patient at risk.\n\nStep 2: Check for responsiveness.\nApproach the patient and try to elicit a response by calling their name and gently shaking their shoulders. If they do not respond, move on to the next step.\n\nStep 3: Call for help.\nIf the patient is unresponsive, call for help immediately. This could be calling for backup or activating the emergency response system in your area.\n\nStep 4: Check for breathing and pulse.\nCheck for breathing by looking for chest rise and fall, and listen for any sounds of breathing. Check for a pulse by feeling for a carotid pulse in the neck.\n\nStep 5: Begin CPR if necessary.\nIf the patient is not breathing and has no pulse, begin CPR immediately. Start with chest compressions and rescue breaths as needed.\n\nBased on these steps, the correct answer is C) Check for response and call help.",
                        "answers": [
