                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: An unresponsive patient may be experiencing a medical emergency such as cardiac arrest, respiratory distress, or neurological issues. It is important to assess the patient's condition and provide appropriate care.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the patient's level of consciousness?\n2. Is the patient breathing?\n3. Does the patient have a pulse?\n\nAnswer:\n1. The first thing to do is to check for response by gently tapping the patient's shoulder and asking if they are okay. If there is no response, call for help immediately.\n2. Check the patient's breathing by looking for chest rise and fall. If the patient is not breathing, start rescue breaths.\n3. Check for a pulse by feeling for the carotid pulse in the neck. If there is no pulse, start chest compressions immediately.",
                        "answers": [
