                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nSchedule H drugs can be sold without a prescription, but only after the pharmacist has recorded the name and address of the purchaser and the name and quantity of the drug sold. Therefore, option A is incorrect.\n\nSchedule G drugs are those that are not covered by the Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985, but still require a prescription. Therefore, option B is incorrect.\n\nSchedule X drugs are those that have a high potential for abuse and addiction and are strictly regulated. They can only be sold with a prescription from a registered medical practitioner with additional requirements such as a special prescription form and a limit on the quantity that can be prescribed. Therefore, option C is correct.\n\nSchedule M drugs are those that are used for the treatment of minor ailments and can be sold without a prescription. Therefore, option D is incorrect.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Schedule X.",
