                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe answer is A) Schedule H.\n\nHere's why:\n\n1. The question is asking which drug must be sold only on production of a prescription by a registered medical practitioner.\n\n2. In India, drugs are classified into different schedules based on their potential for abuse and the level of control required to ensure their safe use.\n\n3. Schedule G drugs are relatively low-risk and can be sold without a prescription, but with certain restrictions.\n\n4. Schedule X drugs are highly addictive and have a high potential for abuse. They can only be sold with a special license and strict controls.\n\n5. Schedule M drugs are those that are manufactured for export and are not intended for sale in India.\n\n6. Schedule H drugs are those that require a prescription from a registered medical practitioner for sale. These drugs have a moderate risk of abuse and require some level of control to ensure their safe use.\n\n7. Therefore, the correct answer is A) Schedule H.",
