s option is a possibility but not the best fit for this case.\n\nStep 3: Choose the best answer.\n\nBased on the key features of the case and the elimination of other options, the best answer is A) Hurler's syndrome. While the age of onset is slightly later than typical, the specific features seen in this case are consistent with Hurler's syndrome, including the coarse facial features, mac",
