                        "cot": "Which of the following conditions is associated with the presence of anti-centromere antibodies?\nA) Drug-induced lupus\nB) Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)\nC) Sjogren syndrome\nD) Scleroderma\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Anti-centromere antibodies are autoantibodies that target the centromere region of chromosomes.\n- These antibodies are associated with certain autoimmune diseases.\n- Drug-induced lupus is not typically associated with the presence of anti-centromere antibodies.\n- SLE is associated with the presence of various autoantibodies, but anti-centromere antibodies are not commonly seen in SLE.\n- Sjogren syndrome is associated with the presence of anti-SSA and anti-SSB antibodies, but not anti-centromere antibodies.\n- Scleroderma is a connective tissue disease that is strongly associated with the presence of anti-centromere antibodies.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Scleroderma.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "2816c56f-c7a9-44de-98e2-303edcef0c20",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
