                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nD) Characterized by sudden decrease in urine volume with increase in urine osmolality dependent of circulating vasopressin levels. \n\nPressor escape is a compensatory mechanism that occurs in some cases of SIADH (syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion) where the body tries to maintain normal blood pressure despite the excess water retention caused by high levels of vasopressin. This mechanism involves the escape of the pressor effect of vasopressin, leading to increased urine output and decreased urine osmolality. However, this escape is not independent of circulating vasopressin levels, as vasopressin still plays a role in regulating water balance in the body.",
