                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Autoinfection refers to the process by which an individual becomes infected with a parasite from their own body, rather than from an external source. Helminths are parasitic worms that can cause a variety of infections in humans.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is Enterobius vermicularis?\n2. Can Enterobius vermicularis cause autoinfection?\n3. What is Hymenolepis nana?\n4. Can Hymenolepis nana cause autoinfection?\n5. What is Taenia solium?\n6. Can Taenia solium cause autoinfection?\n7. What is Ascaris lumbricoides?\n8. Can Ascaris lumbricoides cause autoinfection?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Enterobius vermicularis is a species of parasitic worm that commonly infects humans, causing a condition known as pinworm infection.\n2. Yes, Enterobius vermicularis can cause autoinfection.\n3. Hymenolepis nana is a species of tapeworm that can infect humans.\n4. Yes, Hymenolepis nana can cause autoinfection.\n5. Taenia solium is a species of tapeworm that can infect humans, causing a condition known as taeniasis.\n6. Yes, Taenia solium can cause autoinfection.\n7. Ascaris lumbricoides is a species of roundworm that can infect humans, causing a condition known as ascariasis.\n8. No, Ascaris lumbricoides cannot cause autoinfection.",
