                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking which of the following processes does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nStep 2: Understand the 5' to 3' direction\nThe 5' to 3' direction refers to the direction in which DNA and RNA molecules are synthesized. In this direction, nucleotides are added to the 3' end of the growing strand.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the options\nA) DNA repair: DNA repair can occur in any direction and is not dependent on the 5' to 3' direction. \nB) DNA replication: DNA replication occurs in the 5' to 3' direction, with nucleotides being added to the 3' end of the growing strand. \nC) RNA editing: RNA editing can occur in any direction and is not dependent on the 5' to 3' direction. \nD) Transcription: Transcription occurs in the 5' to 3' direction, with RNA nucleotides being added to the 3' end of the growing RNA strand.\n\nStep 4: Determine the answer\nBased on the analysis, the process that does not occur in the 5' to 3' direction is DNA repair. Therefore, the answer is A) DNA repair.\n\nFinal answer: A) DNA repair.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "f119c2e7-7941-45e5-9f91-e5a9eec8a223",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) DNA repair.",
