                        "cot": "it is important to note that chickenpox infection in a pregnant woman can be dangerous for the baby at any stage of pregnancy. However, the most dangerous time is during the first 20 weeks of pregnancy, particularly between 13-20 weeks. This is because the baby's organs are still developing during this time and the virus can cause birth defects or even miscarriage. Therefore, option D (8-14 weeks) is the closest answer.",
