                        "cot": "What is the most effective way to detect translocation t(ll;22) in Ewing's sarcoma in an eight-year-old child with leg swelling based on a biopsy showing small round blue tumor cells?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Ewing's sarcoma is a type of malignancy that is characterized by a specific genetic abnormality called translocation t(ll;22).\n- Translocation t(ll;22) involves the fusion of two genes, EWSR1 and FLI1, which results in the formation of a chimeric protein that plays a key role in the development of Ewing's sarcoma.\n- Therefore, detecting translocation t(ll;22) is important for the diagnosis and management of Ewing's sarcoma.\n- There are several methods that can be used to detect translocation t(ll;22), including conventional karyotyping, next generation sequencing, FISH, and PCR.\n- Conventional karyotyping involves analyzing the chromosomes of the cancer cells under a microscope to identify any abnormalities, including translocations. However, this method may not be sensitive enough to detect translocation t(ll;22) in all cases.\n- Next generation sequencing is a more advanced technique that can sequence the entire genome of the cancer cells and identify specific genetic abnormalities, including translocations. However, this method may be expensive and time-consuming.\n- FISH (fluorescence in situ hybridization) is a technique that uses fluorescent probes to detect specific DNA sequences, including the fusion of EWSR1 and FLI1 genes in translocation t(ll;22). This method is highly sensitive and specific for detecting translocations.\n- PCR (polymerase chain reaction) is a technique that can amplify specific DNA sequences, including the fusion of EWSR1 and FLI1 genes in translocation t(ll;22). This method is also highly sensitive and specific for detecting translocations.\n\nTherefore, the best method to detect translocation t(ll;22) in Ewing's sarcoma in an eight-year-old child with leg swelling based on a biopsy showing small round blue tumor cells is C) FISH.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e5a15535-dd0b-4daf-81e3-2fe062929adc",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) FISH.",
