                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what non-communicable diseases are. Non-communicable diseases (NCDs) are medical conditions that are not caused by infectious agents and cannot be transmitted from one person to another. Examples of NCDs include heart disease, cancer, diabetes, and chronic respiratory diseases.\n\nNext, we need to understand what the question is asking. The question is asking about a trend in the number of NCD cases over time. Specifically, it is asking about a gradual increase in the number of cases compared to previous years.\n\nNow, we can look at the answer choices. \n\nA) Seasonal: This answer choice does not make sense because NCDs are not typically associated with seasonal patterns.\n\nB) Cyclical: This answer choice also does not make sense because NCDs are not typically associated with cyclical patterns.\n\nC) Periodical: This answer choice is closer to the correct answer, but it still does not quite fit. Periodical implies a regular, predictable pattern, but the question is asking about a gradual increase over time.\n\nD) Secular: This answer choice is the best fit. Secular trends refer to long-term trends that occur over decades or centuries. In the context of NCDs, a secular trend would refer to a gradual increase in the number of cases over time, which is exactly what the question is asking about.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Secular.",
