                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Read the question and the options carefully.\n\nStep 2: Identify the key information in the question - there has been a gradual increase in the number of non-communicable disease cases as compared to previous years.\n\nStep 3: Look at the options and try to eliminate any that are clearly incorrect. \n\n- A) Seasonal: This option refers to changes that occur in a regular pattern over the course of a year. It is unlikely to be the correct answer as the increase in non-communicable disease cases is not likely to be related to seasonal changes.\n- B) Cyclical: This option refers to changes that occur in a regular pattern over a longer period of time. It is possible that the increase in non-communicable disease cases could be cyclical, but there is no information in the question to suggest this.\n- C) Periodical: This option is similar to cyclical and refers to changes that occur in a regular pattern over a period of time. Again, there is no information in the question to suggest this is the correct answer.\n- D) Secular: This option refers to changes that occur over a long period of time, usually decades or centuries. Given that the increase in non-communicable disease cases has been gradual, it is possible that this trend is secular.\n\nStep 4: Based on the information in the question and the options provided, the most likely answer is D) Secular. \n\nStep 5: Double-check your answer to make sure it makes sense in the context of the question. In this case, the increase in non-communicable disease cases over a long period of time is consistent with a secular trend. \n\nFinal answer: D) Secular.",
