                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Internal carotid artery is not ligated in case of epistaxis control as it is a major artery supplying blood to the brain and ligation can lead to serious complications such as stroke or brain damage. The other options, maxillary artery, anterior ethmoidal artery, and external carotid artery, may be ligated in certain cases of severe or recurrent epistaxis.",
