                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The APGAR score is a quick assessment tool used to evaluate the physical condition of a newborn immediately after birth. It was developed by Dr. Virginia Apgar in 1952.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. Who developed the APGAR score?\n2. What is the purpose of the APGAR score?\n3. What does each letter in the APGAR acronym stand for?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Dr. Virginia Apgar developed the APGAR score.\n2. The purpose of the APGAR score is to quickly assess the physical condition of a newborn immediately after birth.\n3. The letters in the APGAR acronym stand for:\n- A: Appearance (skin color)\n- P: Pulse (heart rate)\n- G: Grimace (reflex irritability)\n- A: Activity (muscle tone)\n- R: Respiration (breathing rate and effort)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Activity, pulse pressure, grimace, appearance, rate of respiration.",
