                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, what does the APGAR acronym stand for?\n\nProfessor: APGAR stands for Activity, Pulse pressure, Grimace, Appearance, and Rate of respiration.\n\nStudent: Can you explain each of these components?\n\nProfessor: Sure. Activity refers to the muscle tone of the baby. Pulse pressure refers to the heart rate and blood pressure. Grimace refers to the reflexes of the baby. Appearance refers to the color of the baby's skin. And rate of respiration refers to the baby's breathing.\n\nStudent: How is the APGAR score calculated?\n\nProfessor: Each component is given a score of 0, 1, or 2. The scores are then added up to give a total score out of 10.\n\nStudent: What is a good APGAR score?\n\nProfessor: A score of 7 or above is considered good. A score of 4-6 indicates that the baby needs some assistance, and a score of 3 or below indicates that the baby is in critical condition and requires immediate medical attention.\n\nStudent: Thank you, Professor. I understand it better now.",
