                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Additional facts: The person has a limited income and wants to save as much money as possible without sacrificing too much of their current lifestyle.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How much money does the person need to save for their vacation?\n2. How much money is the person currently spending on phone calls?\n3. How much money is the person currently spending on eating lunch out?\n4. What is the value of monopoly money to the person?\n5. How often does the person have lunch with friends?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The person needs to determine the cost of the vacation they want to take in order to know how much money they need to save.\n2. If the person is spending a significant amount of money on phone calls, they could consider finding a cheaper phone plan or using a free communication app to save money.\n3. If the person is spending a lot of money on eating lunch out, they could consider bringing their own lunch from home or finding cheaper lunch options.\n4. If the person is using monopoly money as a way to budget their expenses, they should convert the value of the monopoly money to real money in order to accurately track their spending and savings.\n5. If the person is having lunch with friends frequently and spending a lot of money on those outings, they could consider having lunch with friends less often or finding cheaper lunch options when they do go out.",
