                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "How can one accurately predict a baby's eye color?\nA) Consider the environment they are born into.\nB) Take into account the typical diet of their parents.\nC) Make a random guess.\nD) Examine the genealogy records of their family.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- A) The surroundings they are born in: While the environment a baby is born into can affect their health and development, it is unlikely to have an impact on their eye color.\n- B) Their parents usual diet: While a person's diet can affect their health and physical appearance, there is no evidence to suggest that a parent's diet can influence their child's eye color.\n- C) Just take a random guess: This is not a reliable method for predicting a baby's eye color.\n- D) The genealogy records of their family: Eye color is largely determined by genetics, so examining the eye color of the baby's parents and other family members can provide a good indication of what color the baby's eyes will be.\n\nThe correct answer is D) The genealogy records of their family.",
