                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Eye color is determined by genetics and is inherited from parents.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are the possible eye colors a baby can have?\n2. How is eye color inherited?\n3. What are the eye colors of the baby's parents?\n4. Are there any other family members with similar eye colors?\n5. Is there a way to predict the likelihood of a baby having a certain eye color based on their parents' eye colors?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The possible eye colors a baby can have are blue, green, brown, hazel, and gray.\n2. Eye color is inherited through a combination of genes from both parents.\n3. Knowing the eye colors of the baby's parents can give an indication of what eye color the baby may have. For example, if both parents have brown eyes, it is more likely that the baby will have brown eyes as well.\n4. Looking at the eye colors of other family members can also give an indication of what eye color the baby may have. If there are several family members with blue eyes, it is more likely that the baby will have blue eyes as well.\n5. There are online eye color calculators that can predict the likelihood of a baby having a certain eye color based on their parents' eye colors. However, these predictions are not always accurate as there are many factors that can influence eye color. The best way to guess a baby's eye color is to look at the eye colors of their parents and other family members and make an educated guess based on that information.",
                        "answers": [
