                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The human body has five senses - sight, hearing, taste, smell, and touch. The sense of sight is responsible for detecting visual stimuli.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What part of the eye is responsible for sensing visual things?\n2. How does the eye detect visual stimuli?\n\nAnswer:\n1. The cornea, lens, and retina are the parts of the eye responsible for sensing visual things.\n2. The cornea and lens focus light onto the retina, which contains photoreceptor cells called rods and cones. These cells convert light into electrical signals that are sent to the brain via the optic nerve, where they are interpreted as visual images. Therefore, option D, cornea, is the correct answer.",
