                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "It is important to know that a pond is a body of water that is typically fed by rainwater or a natural spring. It is also important to know that heavy rainfall can cause a pond to overflow or flood.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens to a pond after heavy rainfall?\n2. What are the possible effects of heavy rainfall on a pond?\n3. How can heavy rainfall affect the water level of a pond?\n\nAnswer:\n1. After heavy rainfall, a pond can overflow or flood.\n2. The possible effects of heavy rainfall on a pond include an increase in water level, a change in water quality, and erosion of the pond's banks.\n3. Heavy rainfall can cause the water level of a pond to rise, which can lead to flooding. This can be dangerous for nearby homes and structures. Additionally, heavy rainfall can cause erosion of the pond's banks, which can lead to the loss of soil and vegetation. This can also affect the water quality of the pond, as sediment and other pollutants can be washed into the water.",
                        "answers": [
