                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Crop rotation is the practice of growing different crops in the same area in sequential seasons to improve soil health and reduce pests and diseases.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How does crop rotation improve soil health?\n2. How does crop rotation reduce pests and diseases?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Crop rotation improves soil health by:\n- Reducing soil erosion: Different crops have different root structures, and rotating crops can help prevent soil erosion by keeping the soil anchored.\n- Increasing soil fertility: Different crops have different nutrient requirements, and rotating crops can help replenish soil nutrients by alternating between crops that deplete certain nutrients and crops that add nutrients back into the soil.\n- Reducing soil compaction: Different crops have different root depths, and rotating crops can help prevent soil compaction by breaking up the soil and allowing air and water to penetrate deeper.\n2. Crop rotation reduces pests and diseases by:\n- Disrupting pest and disease life cycles: Different crops attract different pests and diseases, and rotating crops can help break the life cycles of these pests and diseases by depriving them of their preferred host plants.\n- Building up beneficial organisms: Different crops attract different beneficial organisms, such as insects and microbes, that can help control pests and diseases. Rotating crops can help build up these beneficial organisms by providing them with a variety of host plants.",
