                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what crop rotation is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, crop rotation is the practice of growing different crops in the same area in sequential seasons or years.\n\nStudent: How does crop rotation have a positive impact on dirt quality?\n\nProfessor: Well, different crops have different nutrient requirements and deplete the soil of different nutrients. By rotating crops, the soil has a chance to replenish the nutrients that were depleted by the previous crop. This helps maintain soil fertility and improves soil quality.\n\nStudent: Does crop rotation have any impact on government mentality?\n\nProfessor: No, crop rotation does not have any direct impact on government mentality.\n\nStudent: What about town economies?\n\nProfessor: Yes, crop rotation can have a positive impact on town economies. By rotating crops, farmers can diversify their crops and increase their yields. This can lead to increased profits and economic growth in the surrounding towns.\n\nStudent: Does crop rotation have any impact on crop watering?\n\nProfessor: Yes, crop rotation can have an indirect impact on crop watering. By improving soil quality and fertility, crops are better able to absorb water and nutrients from the soil. This can lead to more efficient use of water and potentially reduce the amount of water needed for irrigation.",
