                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Original question: What happens when you bang on a drum?\n\nHelpful knowledge: A drum is a percussion instrument that produces sound when struck with a drumstick or hand. The sound is created by the vibration of the drumhead and the air inside the drum.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. How does banging on a drum produce sound?\n2. What is the effect of the sound produced by a drum?\n3. What happens to the sound after it is produced?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Banging on a drum produces sound by causing the drumhead to vibrate. The vibration creates sound waves that travel through the air and into the ear.\n2. The effect of the sound produced by a drum is loud and percussive. It can be used to create rhythm and melody in music.\n3. After the sound is produced, it travels through the air and into the ear. The sound waves cause the eardrum to vibrate, which sends signals to the brain that are interpreted as sound. The sound also bounces off surfaces in the environment, creating reverberations that can add depth and richness to the sound.",
