                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Read the question and the answer choices carefully.\n\nStep 2: Identify the key terms in the question and the answer choices. The key terms in the question are \"cells\" and \"cellular respiration.\" The key terms in the answer choices are \"photosynthesize,\" \"release waste,\" \"perform meiosis,\" and \"release energy.\"\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer by eliminating the incorrect answer choices. \n\nOption A: Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy. This process is not used by all cells, so option A is incorrect.\n\nOption B: Releasing waste is a function of excretion, which is the process of eliminating metabolic waste products from the body. While all cells produce waste, not all cells release waste, so option B is incorrect.\n\nOption C: Meiosis is a type of cell division that produces gametes (sex cells) with half the number of chromosomes as the parent cell. This process is not used by all cells, so option C is incorrect.\n\nOption D: Cellular respiration is the process by which cells convert glucose and oxygen into energy, carbon dioxide, and water. This process is used by all cells to release energy, so option D is correct.\n\nStep 4: Verify the answer. All cells use cellular respiration to release energy, so option D is the correct answer.",
