                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Seasons refer to the changes in weather patterns and temperature that occur in a cyclical manner throughout the year. \n\nAdditional facts: The Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of approximately 23.5 degrees relative to its orbit around the sun. This tilt causes different parts of the Earth to receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year, which in turn affects the weather patterns and temperature.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the Earth's axis?\nAnswer: The Earth's axis is an imaginary line that runs through the center of the Earth from the North Pole to the South Pole.\n\n2. What is the angle of the Earth's axis relative to its orbit around the sun?\nAnswer: The Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of approximately 23.5 degrees relative to its orbit around the sun.\n\n3. What causes different parts of the Earth to receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year?\nAnswer: The tilt of the Earth's axis causes different parts of the Earth to receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year.\n\nAnswer: D) The Sun is what causes seasons by shining on different parts of the Earth at different angles due to the Earth's tilt on its axis.",
