                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The original question is not clear. It is unclear what the question is asking for. Therefore, we will generate a new question based on the given information.\n\nWhat are some common allergic reactions caused by medicine?\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is an allergic reaction?\n2. How do medicines cause allergic reactions?\n3. What are some common symptoms of allergic reactions caused by medicine?\n\nAnswers:\n1. An allergic reaction is a response by the immune system to a foreign substance that is not typically harmful to the body.\n2. Medicines can cause allergic reactions by triggering an immune response in the body.\n3. Common symptoms of allergic reactions caused by medicine include hives, itching, swelling, difficulty breathing, and anaphylaxis. \n\nTherefore, some common allergic reactions caused by medicine are hives, itching, swelling, difficulty breathing, and anaphylaxis.",
