                        "cot": "How can we find water in its gas form?\n\nA) Can water be found in its gas form inside a disc golf driver?\nB) Can water be found in its gas form inside of a brass pipe?\nC) Can water be found in its gas form a mile up in the sky?\nD) Can water be found in its gas form inside a leather baseball?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\nA) It is unlikely that water can be found in its gas form inside a disc golf driver as it is a solid object and not a container for gas.\nB) It is possible that water can be found in its gas form inside of a brass pipe if the pipe is heated and the water inside evaporates into gas.\nC) It is likely that water can be found in its gas form a mile up in the sky as it can evaporate from bodies of water on the ground and rise into the atmosphere.\nD) It is unlikely that water can be found in its gas form inside a leather baseball as it is a solid object and not a container for gas.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) a mile up in the sky.",
