                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What could be the reason for a perennial plant with a long stem, often used for lumber, to fall to the ground?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Perennial plants are those that live for more than two years.\n- A plant with an elongated stem could be a tree or a tall shrub.\n- Lumber is wood that has been processed for construction or other uses.\n- If a plant falls to the ground, it means that it is no longer upright and supported by its roots.\n- The question asks for the reason why this could happen.\n\nAnswer: A) It's dead. \n- If a plant is dead, its roots can no longer support its weight, and it will fall to the ground.\n- None of the other options (B, C, D) would necessarily cause a plant to fall to the ground.",
