                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) only happens in the summer - This is incorrect. Evaporation can happen in any season, as long as there is water present and the temperature is high enough.\n\nB) is like nature's disappearing water trick - This is a good description of evaporation. When water evaporates, it seems to disappear into thin air, leaving behind only dryness.\n\nC) is caused by snow - This is incorrect. Snow is a form of precipitation, which is the opposite of evaporation. Evaporation is caused by heat, which causes water molecules to become more energetic and break free from the surface of a liquid.\n\nD) involves the disappearance of sunlight - This is not entirely accurate. While sunlight can certainly contribute to evaporation by providing heat, it is not the only factor. Other factors that can affect evaporation include humidity, wind, and the surface area of the water.",
