                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Determine what evaporation is.\n2. Identify the cause of evaporation.\n3. Determine if evaporation only happens in the summer.\n4. Determine if evaporation is like nature's disappearing water trick.\n5. Determine if evaporation is caused by snow.\n6. Determine if evaporation involves the disappearance of sunlight.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. Evaporation is the process by which a liquid, such as water, changes into a gas or vapor.\n2. The cause of evaporation is heat, which causes the molecules in the liquid to gain energy and become more active, eventually breaking free from the liquid and becoming a gas.\n3. The statement \"evaporation only happens in the summer\" is false. Evaporation can happen at any time of the year, as long as there is enough heat to cause it.\n4. The statement \"evaporation is like nature's disappearing water trick\" is true. When water evaporates, it seems to disappear, as it turns into a gas and becomes invisible to the naked eye.\n5. The statement \"evaporation is caused by snow\" is false. Snow is a solid form of water, and while it can eventually turn into water and then evaporate, it is not the cause of evaporation.\n6. The statement \"evaporation involves the disappearance of sunlight\" is false. While sunlight can provide the heat necessary for evaporation to occur, it is not necessary for evaporation to happen. Heat from any source can cause evaporation.",
