                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: What is evaporation and what causes it?\n\nHelpful knowledge: Evaporation is the process by which a liquid turns into a gas or vapor. It occurs when the molecules of a liquid gain enough energy to break free from the surface and become a gas. Evaporation is an important part of the water cycle and occurs naturally in the environment.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the definition of evaporation?\n2. How does evaporation occur?\n3. Is evaporation a natural process?\n4. What is the role of evaporation in the water cycle?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Evaporation is the process by which a liquid turns into a gas or vapor.\n2. Evaporation occurs when the molecules of a liquid gain enough energy to break free from the surface and become a gas.\n3. Yes, evaporation is a natural process that occurs in the environment.\n4. Evaporation is an important part of the water cycle as it allows water to move from the surface of the Earth into the atmosphere, where it can form clouds and eventually fall back to the Earth as precipitation.",
