                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Muscles are responsible for producing movement in the body by contracting and relaxing. They are attached to bones via tendons and work in pairs to produce movement in opposite directions.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What muscles are responsible for moving the arms?\n2. What muscles are responsible for hair growth?\n3. What muscles are responsible for producing a smile?\n4. What muscles are responsible for wiggling toes?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The muscles responsible for moving the arms are the biceps and triceps. When the biceps contract, the arm bends at the elbow, and when the triceps contract, the arm straightens.\n2. Hair growth is not directly controlled by muscles. It is a natural process that occurs as hair follicles produce new hair cells.\n3. The muscles responsible for producing a smile are the zygomaticus major and minor muscles. When these muscles contract, they pull the corners of the mouth upward, producing a smile.\n4. The muscles responsible for wiggling toes are the flexor digitorum brevis and the lumbricals. When these muscles contract, they pull the toes downward and curl them.",
