                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain how muscles move bones to produce movement?\n\nProfessor: Sure. When muscles contract, they pull on the bones they are attached to, causing them to move.\n\nStudent: How do muscles contract?\n\nProfessor: Muscles contract when they receive a signal from the nervous system. This signal causes the muscle fibers to shorten and pull on the bones they are attached to.\n\nStudent: What happens when the muscle fibers shorten?\n\nProfessor: When the muscle fibers shorten, they pull on the tendons that are attached to the bones. This causes the bones to move.\n\nStudent: So, when we wiggle our toes, the muscles in our feet are contracting and pulling on the tendons that are attached to our toe bones?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. When we wiggle our toes, the muscles in our feet are contracting and pulling on the tendons that are attached to our toe bones, causing them to move.",
