                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Air is a mixture of gases that surrounds the Earth and is held in place by gravity. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is required for something to travel through the air?\n2. Are planets capable of traveling through the air?\n3. Are thoughts capable of traveling through the air?\n4. Are automobiles capable of traveling through the air?\n5. Is music capable of traveling through the air?\n\nAnswers:\n1. For something to travel through the air, it must be a physical object that is light enough to be lifted by air currents or propelled through the air by a force.\n2. Planets are not capable of traveling through the air as they are massive celestial bodies that are held in orbit by gravity.\n3. Thoughts are not physical objects and therefore cannot travel through the air.\n4. Automobiles are capable of traveling through the air if they are lifted off the ground by a force such as a ramp or a jump.\n5. Music is capable of traveling through the air as it is a form of sound that can be transmitted through air molecules as vibrations. \n\nAnswer: D) Music travels through the air.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "2bb211f1-e7c9-4ac9-b9f7-3452d658527d",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
