                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Electrical devices require a source of electricity to turn on.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a solar-rechargeable battery?\n2. How does a solar-rechargeable battery work?\n3. Can a solar-rechargeable battery be used to turn on an electrical device?\n4. What is a wedge?\n5. How does a wedge work?\n6. Can a wedge be used to turn on an electrical device?\n7. What is a magnet?\n8. How does a magnet work?\n9. Can a magnet be used to turn on an electrical device?\n10. What is a pressure gauge?\n11. How does a pressure gauge work?\n12. Can a pressure gauge be used to turn on an electrical device?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A solar-rechargeable battery is a type of battery that can be recharged using solar energy.\n2. A solar-rechargeable battery works by converting solar energy into electrical energy, which is stored in the battery.\n3. Yes, a solar-rechargeable battery can be used to turn on an electrical device.\n4. A wedge is a simple machine that is used to lift or separate objects.\n5. A wedge works by applying force to an object, causing it to move in a specific direction.\n6. No, a wedge cannot be used to turn on an electrical device.\n7. A magnet is an object that produces a magnetic field.\n8. A magnet works by attracting or repelling other magnets or magnetic materials.\n9. Yes, a magnet can be used to turn on an electrical device if the device has a magnetic switch.\n10. A pressure gauge is a device that measures the pressure of a fluid or gas.\n11. A pressure gauge works by measuring the force exerted by the fluid or gas on a surface.\n12. No, a pressure gauge cannot be used to turn on an electrical device.",
