                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: How can we see how wind effects sand?\n\nProfessor: Well, there are a few ways we can observe this. One way is to look at how sand is always moving.\n\nStudent: How does that show us how wind affects sand?\n\nProfessor: When wind blows over sand, it causes the sand particles to move and shift. This movement is what we see when we observe sand always moving.\n\nStudent: Okay, that makes sense. What about sandstorms?\n\nProfessor: Sandstorms are another way we can see how wind affects sand. During a sandstorm, the wind is blowing so hard that it creates ripples in the sand.\n\nStudent: So, the ripples are caused by the wind?\n\nProfessor: Yes, exactly. The wind is blowing the sand particles around, and as they move, they create these ripples.\n\nStudent: I see. What about the texture of sand? Does that have anything to do with how wind affects it?\n\nProfessor: Yes, actually. Sand is easy to move through, which means that wind can easily pick it up and move it around. This is why we often see sand dunes in areas with strong winds.\n\nStudent: That's interesting. And what about beaches? How can we see how wind affects sand there?\n\nProfessor: Beaches often have waves in the sand, which are caused by the wind blowing over the surface. These waves can give us an idea of how strong the wind is and in what direction it's blowing.",
