                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Leaves are the primary site of photosynthesis in plants, where they produce glucose and oxygen from carbon dioxide and water using energy from sunlight.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is photosynthesis?\n2. What are the products of photosynthesis?\n3. What is the role of leaves in photosynthesis?\n4. What other processes occur in leaves besides photosynthesis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.\n2. The products of photosynthesis are glucose and oxygen.\n3. Leaves are the primary site of photosynthesis in plants, where they use energy from sunlight to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen.\n4. Besides photosynthesis, leaves also perform respiration, which is the process by which cells break down glucose to release energy, and transpiration, which is the loss of water vapor from the leaves. However, digestion does not occur in leaves as they do not have a digestive system.",
