                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Identify what fire is and how it produces light.\n2. Think of examples where fire is used or seen in everyday life.\n3. Determine which examples involve fire giving off light.\n\nAnswer: \nFire is a chemical reaction that produces heat and light. When fuel (such as wood or gas) combines with oxygen and heat, it creates a flame that emits light. Examples of fire giving off light include a lit candle in a window signaling to someone (option C). While options A and B involve fire, they do not necessarily give off light. Option D involves smoke signals, which are created by burning material, but do not involve fire giving off light.",
