                    {
                        "id": "c1c3d9ed-8ca4-43de-bcfe-d401aa91ca06",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Fire is a chemical reaction that produces heat, light, and various gases. The light produced by fire is a result of the energy released during the chemical reaction.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is fire?\n2. How does fire produce light?\n3. What are some examples of fire giving off light?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Fire is a chemical reaction that occurs when a fuel source (such as wood or gasoline) combines with oxygen in the air and is ignited by a heat source (such as a spark or flame).\n2. Fire produces light through a process called incandescence, which is the emission of light from a hot object. As the fuel source burns, it releases energy in the form of heat and light. The heat causes the fuel to glow, emitting light in the process.\n3. Examples of fire giving off light include: \n- A match being lit to light a cigarette: When the match is struck, the heat generated by the friction ignites the chemicals on the match head, causing a flame to form. The flame produces light as it burns.\n- A lit candle in a window signaling to someone: When a candle is lit, the heat of the flame melts the wax, which is drawn up the wick by capillary action. The heat also causes the wax vapor to ignite, producing a flame that gives off light.\n- An oven being preheated and the pilot light being lit: When an oven is preheated, the heating element or gas burner produces heat, which causes the air inside the oven to heat up. If the oven is gas-powered, a pilot light ignites the gas to produce a flame, which gives off light.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0dfe8174-6a36-41e6-8481-81fae17215b9",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) a lit candle in a window signaling to someone.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "C",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 04:50:03",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-3.5-turbo', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
