                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step-by-step procedure:\n1. Identify the energy sources listed.\n2. Research the pollution levels associated with each energy source.\n3. Compare the pollution levels to determine which energy source generates the least amount of pollution.\n\nGoing through each step:\n1. The energy sources listed are coal, windmill, lithium batteries, and gasoline.\n2. Coal is known to generate a significant amount of pollution, including greenhouse gases, particulate matter, and sulfur dioxide. Windmills generate no pollution during operation, but there may be some pollution associated with their manufacturing and disposal. Lithium batteries can generate pollution during their manufacturing and disposal, but they do not generate pollution during operation. Gasoline generates pollution during operation, including carbon monoxide, nitrogen oxides, and particulate matter.\n3. Comparing the pollution levels, windmills generate the least amount of pollution during operation, followed by lithium batteries. Coal generates the most pollution, and gasoline generates a significant amount of pollution as well. Therefore, the answer is B) windmill.",
