                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Among the given energy sources, which one produces the least pollution?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Coal is a fossil fuel that releases a significant amount of carbon dioxide and other harmful pollutants when burned. Therefore, it is not the answer.\n- Windmills generate electricity by harnessing the power of wind, which is a renewable and clean source of energy. Windmills do not produce any pollution, so it is a possible answer.\n- Lithium batteries store energy and can power various devices, but they do not generate energy themselves. Therefore, they are not the answer.\n- Gasoline is a fossil fuel that powers most vehicles and machinery. It releases carbon dioxide and other pollutants when burned, making it a significant contributor to air pollution. Therefore, it is not the answer.\n\nConclusion: The answer is B) windmill, as it is the only energy source among the given options that does not produce any pollution.",
