                    {
                        "id": "02223e98-5e23-4f08-9f31-9c9dfa397775",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Pollution is the presence or introduction into the environment of contaminants or substances that cause harm or discomfort to living organisms. Different energy sources have different impacts on the environment and can generate varying amounts of pollution.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What types of pollution are typically associated with energy sources?\n2. How does coal generate energy?\n3. How does a windmill generate energy?\n4. How are lithium batteries used as an energy source?\n5. How does gasoline generate energy?\n6. Which energy source generates the least amount of pollution?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Different energy sources can generate different types of pollution, including air pollution, water pollution, and soil pollution. \n2. Coal generates energy by burning coal to heat water and produce steam, which then drives turbines to generate electricity. This process releases large amounts of carbon dioxide, sulfur dioxide, nitrogen oxides, and particulate matter into the air, making it a significant source of air pollution. \n3. A windmill generates energy by harnessing the power of wind to turn turbines, which then generate electricity. This process does not produce any emissions or pollution, making it a clean energy source. \n4. Lithium batteries are typically used to store energy generated by other sources, such as solar or wind power. While the production of lithium batteries can generate some pollution, their use as an energy source does not produce any emissions or pollution. \n5. Gasoline generates energy by burning gasoline in an engine to power vehicles or machinery. This process releases carbon monoxide, nitrogen oxides, and volatile organic compounds into the air, making it a significant source of air pollution. \n6. Based on the information above, the windmill generates the least amount of pollution as it does not produce any emissions or pollution during its operation.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "128afad2-4ad6-4d8d-b964-bf86ca4f6757",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) windmill.",
                                "answer_from_choices": "B",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/30 04:50:18",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-3.5-turbo', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
