                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is asking what causes erosion. Erosion is the process of wearing away or breaking down materials, such as soil or rock, through natural forces. \n\nOption A, soil, cannot be the cause of erosion because erosion is the result of soil being eroded, not the cause of it. \n\nOption B, fish, is not a likely cause of erosion as fish do not have the ability to wear away or break down materials on a large scale. \n\nOption C, rocks, can be a cause of erosion as they can be broken down by natural forces such as wind, water, and ice. However, rocks alone are not the only cause of erosion. \n\nOption D, weather, is the most likely cause of erosion as it includes natural forces such as wind, water, and ice that can wear away or break down materials over time. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) weather.",
                        "answers": [
