                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Distance: Echolocation is a process where animals emit sound waves and then listen to the echoes that bounce back to them. Based on the time it takes for the echo to return, animals can determine the distance of an object. Therefore, echolocation can detect an object's distance. \n\nB) Shape: Echolocation can also detect an object's shape. By analyzing the echoes that bounce back, animals can determine the shape of an object. \n\nC) Size: Echolocation can also detect an object's size. By analyzing the strength of the echoes that bounce back, animals can determine the size of an object. \n\nD) Temperature: Echolocation cannot detect an object's temperature. \n\nCombining all the information, we can conclude that the correct answer is D) Temperature. \n\nTherefore, the answer is D) Temperature.",
