                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose. This process requires certain ingredients to occur.\n\nAdditional facts: CO2 is carbon dioxide, H20 is water, and argon is a noble gas that is not involved in photosynthesis. Fertilizer is not an ingredient in photosynthesis, but it can provide nutrients for plant growth.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is photosynthesis?\n2. What are the necessary ingredients for photosynthesis?\n3. What is the role of each ingredient in photosynthesis?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Photosynthesis is the process by which plants, algae, and some bacteria convert light energy into chemical energy in the form of glucose.\n2. The necessary ingredients for photosynthesis are carbon dioxide (CO2), water (H20), and sunlight.\n3. CO2 is used by plants to make glucose, while water is used to provide hydrogen ions and electrons. Sunlight provides the energy needed to power the chemical reactions that convert CO2 and H20 into glucose.",
