                        "cot": "Additional fact: A sousaphone is a musical instrument.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is a sousaphone?\n2. How does a sousaphone produce sound?\n3. What is the history of the sousaphone?\n\nAnswers:\n1. A sousaphone is a brass instrument that is similar to a tuba. It is commonly used in marching bands and has a large, flared bell that faces forward.\n2. A sousaphone produces sound by the musician buzzing their lips into a mouthpiece, which creates vibrations that travel through the instrument and out of the bell.\n3. The sousaphone was invented by John Philip Sousa in the late 19th century as a way to improve the sound of the tuba in marching bands. It was designed to be easier to carry and play while marching.",
