                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: What is the importance of prey for carnivores?\n\nHelpful knowledge: Carnivores are animals that primarily eat meat. They are often at the top of the food chain and play an important role in maintaining the balance of ecosystems.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are carnivores?\n2. What is the food chain?\n3. Where do carnivores typically fall on the food chain?\n4. What role do carnivores play in ecosystems?\n5. Why do carnivores require prey to survive?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Carnivores are animals that primarily eat meat.\n2. The food chain is a hierarchical series of organisms in an ecosystem, where each organism is dependent on the one below it for food.\n3. Carnivores are often at the top of the food chain, as they are predators that consume other animals.\n4. Carnivores play an important role in maintaining the balance of ecosystems by controlling the populations of their prey and preventing overgrazing or overpopulation.\n5. Carnivores require prey to survive because they need the nutrients and energy that are found in meat. They are not able to produce their own food like plants, so they must consume other organisms to obtain the necessary nutrients.",
